## Why This Is Asked
 Tests ability to design a scalable, multi-tenant privacy enforcement and incident response workflow on GCP, including data lineage, per-tenant isolation, and automated remediation under real-time load.

## Key Concepts
 - Real-time data processing, per-tenant isolation, data masking, DLP, Vertex AI, Dataflow, Pub/Sub, Data Catalog lineage
 - Event-time vs processing-time semantics, idempotency, backpressure, rollback strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
function maskPII(record){
  const r = { ...record };
  if (r.ssn) r.ssn = '***-**-****';
  if (r.email) r.email = r.email.replace(/(.{1})(.*)(@)/, '$1***$2$3');
  return r;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the anomaly model under bursty traffic and schema drift?
- How would you handle false positives/negatives and post-incident cleanup?

## Why This Is Asked
Probes multi-tenant data integrity, privacy, and governance at scale, including schema drift handling, masking, and lineage.

## Key Concepts
- Schema registry in Cloud Storage and Drift detection in Dataflow/Beam
- Row-level security with BigQuery policies for per-tenant isolation
- Per-tenant DLP masking and quarantine of invalid data
- Data Catalog lineage and end-to-end observability

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-Beam DoFn skeleton for schema validation
class ValidateSchema extends DoFn {
  processElement(context) {
    const record = context.element;
    // load canonical schema from GCS
    // validate fields, types, requireds
    if (valid(record)) {
      context.output(record);
    } else {
      context.output(NOT_VALID, record);
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test schema drift in production without impacting traffic?
- How would you implement rollback across tenants if a schema change breaks downstream queries?
